From 2a672cdc562886fad30d560c6a268cf1afd5e6ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 09:59:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00448/11362] [outer-loop] Fix GitHub Pages build: remove
 orphaned ebt_tmp submodule gitlink
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every GitHub Pages build was failing at the Checkout step with:
  fatal: No url found for submodule path 'ebt_tmp' in .gitmodules
  git failed with exit code 128

Root cause: the vendored EBT repo (ebt_tmp/, which has its own .git) was committed
as a submodule gitlink (mode 160000) with no .gitmodules entry. GitHub's
pages-build-deployment workflow runs `git submodule update --init --recursive`,
which dies on the orphaned gitlink — failing every Pages build instantly (duration 0,
generic "Page build failed"). The last successful Pages build predated this commit
reaching GitHub. Untracked the gitlink (ebt_tmp stays on disk) and gitignored it so
the conductor's `git add -A` can't reintroduce it. This unblocks Pages (and publishes
the blog post + ~143 commits of site updates that were stuck behind it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .gitignore | 4 ++++
 ebt_tmp    | 1 -
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 delete mode 160000 ebt_tmp

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index b54fd2fccd..7d3dcc1262 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -142,3 +142,7 @@ tests/python/test_conductor_supervisor.py
 
 # Conductor pre-test fingerprint cache — local-only, regenerated on first run
 ops/.pretest-cache.json
+
+# Vendored EBT repo (has its own .git) — must NOT be committed as a submodule gitlink;
+# an orphaned ebt_tmp gitlink with no .gitmodules broke every GitHub Pages build (checkout step).
+ebt_tmp/
diff --git a/ebt_tmp b/ebt_tmp
deleted file mode 160000
index 19420cbeae..0000000000
--- a/ebt_tmp
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1 +0,0 @@
-Subproject commit 19420cbeae655bbf11930219a675ade6897019e8
